        "content": "# Quick Build: Add Json Validation\n\n**Created**: 2026-02-24T00:00:00Z\n**Request**: add a json validation script that's ultra performant\n**Scope**: Small\n\n## Plan\n\n**Reasoning**: This is an additive feature touching 2-3 files in a single system (utility/script layer). No existing code needs modification beyond optionally registering a new script in package.json. Risk is low since this is purely new code with no coupling to existing logic.\n\n**Files Affected**:\n- `src/validate-json.ts` (new -- core validation module)\n- `src/validate-json.test.ts` (new -- test suite)\n- `package.json` (minor update -- add a `validate` script entry)\n\n**Approach**: Implement a high-performance JSON validation script in TypeScript targeting the Bun runtime. The validator will use a single-pass streaming approach with manual character-by-character state-machine parsing rather than relying on `JSON.parse` with try/catch, which allocates an entire object graph just to check validity. The script will accept input via stdin or file path argument, report validation errors with line/column positions, and exit with appropriate codes. Performance will be verified with a benchmark in the test file comparing against naive `JSON.parse` for large payloads.\n\n**Estimated Effort**: 1.5 hours\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Create `src/validate-json.ts` with a state-machine-based JSON validator that walks input bytes without constructing an object tree, supporting all JSON grammar rules (strings with escapes, numbers, booleans, null, nested objects/arrays) and returning structured error results with byte offset `[complexity:medium]`\n- [ ] **T2**: Add CLI entrypoint logic to `src/validate-json.ts` that reads from a file path argument or stdin, runs the validator, prints results, and exits with code 0 (valid) or 1 (invalid) `[complexity:simple]`\n- [ ] **T3**: Create `src/validate-json.test.ts` with unit tests covering valid JSON (objects, arrays, nested, edge cases like empty containers and unicode escapes), invalid JSON (trailing commas, single quotes, unquoted keys, truncated input), and a performance benchmark asserting the validator handles a 1MB payload in under 50ms `[complexity:medium]`\n- [ ] **T4**: Update `package.json` to add a `\"validate\"` script entry pointing to `bun run src/validate-json.ts` `[complexity:simple]`\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n{To be added by task-builder}\n\n## Verification\n\n{To be added by task-reviewer if --review flag used}\n"
